The point here is that exposure to a $300M _gain_ is very, very different from exposure
to a $300M _loss_. If we had $3B in the bank, we would have a different loss function and
might be happy to take that bet, but right now losing it would be existential.

Running the simulated NPV distribution through our loss function allows us to consider
the project again, but this time placed into the important context of our company's
loss tolerance.

